.spec/decisions.md-4-| --- | --- | --- |
.spec/decisions.md-5-| ADR-001 | Accepted | Build a system VPN around `NEPacketTunnelProvider`; keep the live SSH transport inside the extension |
.spec/decisions.md-6-| ADR-002 | Accepted | Use HEV/lwIP instead of writing a TCP/IP stack |
.spec/decisions.md-7-| ADR-003 | Accepted | Bridge `NEPacketTunnelFlow` through a public nonblocking `AF_UNIX/SOCK_DGRAM` socket pair; do not discover the utun FD |
.spec/decisions.md:8:| ADR-004 | Accepted | Fix HEV's internal UDP mode to UDP-in-TCP and reuse its datagram address framing |
.spec/decisions.md:9:| ADR-005 | Accepted | Use SSH `direct-tcpip` for TCP and a rootless exec/stdio relay for UDP |
.spec/decisions.md:10:| ADR-006 | Accepted | Upload the relay through exec stdin; do not add SFTP to `SSHTransport` |
.spec/decisions.md:11:| ADR-007 | Accepted | Support full and degraded TCP + safe-DNS modes instead of failing solely because UDP relay is unavailable |
.spec/decisions.md-12-| ADR-008 | Accepted | Use 2–4 SSH lanes, pin live flows, and assign only new flows using congestion-aware policy |
.spec/decisions.md-13-| ADR-009 | Accepted | Treat channel windows, lane count, HEV limits, and reconnect overlap as one memory budget |
.spec/decisions.md-14-| ADR-010 | Accepted | Expose configurable QUIC behavior; default `Auto` may force a fast TCP fallback |
.spec/decisions.md:15:| ADR-011 | Accepted | Develop packet/SSH/relay core through an SPM macOS harness while proving packetFlow, lifecycle, and memory on physical iPhone |
.spec/decisions.md-16-| ADR-012 | Accepted | Make compatible and platform-scoped fail-closed route modes explicit user choices |
.spec/decisions.md-17-| ADR-013 | Gate | Obtain evidence that local TCP termination + remote `direct-tcpip` is acceptable under Apple's packet-tunnel intended-use guidance |
.spec/decisions.md-18-| ADR-014 | Open | Select a minimal SwiftNIO SSH fork or libssh2 only after per-channel windows, rekey, compatibility, memory, and lifecycle tests |
.spec/decisions.md-19-| ADR-015 | Open | Select the production MTU from physical-device tests of 1500, 4096, and 8500 |
.spec/decisions.md:20:| ADR-016 | Accepted | Set new Apple targets to iOS 18.0 and macOS 15.0; preserve the legacy SwiftPM product at macOS 14.0; require minimum/current CI plus named physical baselines per TASK-260715-3r0993 |
.spec/decisions.md-21-| ADR-017 | Accepted | Use Tuist 4.202.5 pinned exactly by repository-local Mise; generate with an explicit Xcode pin and deterministic graph/project comparison per TASK-260715-3r0993 |
.spec/decisions.md:22:| ADR-018 | Accepted | Ship macOS in-app self-update via Sparkle 2.x with an EdDSA-signed appcast; every payload is an already-notarized Developer ID build; iOS updates stay with the App Store |
