.spec/relay-protocol.md-94-
.spec/relay-protocol.md:95:`UDP_DATAGRAM` reuses the HEV UDP-in-TCP relay layout:
.spec/relay-protocol.md-96-
.spec/relay-protocol.md-97-```text
.spec/relay-protocol.md-98-MSGLEN:u16 | HDRLEN:u8 | ATYP:u8 | DST.ADDR:variable | DST.PORT:u16 | DATA:variable
.spec/relay-protocol.md-99-```
.spec/relay-protocol.md-100-
.spec/relay-protocol.md-101-`MSGLEN` and `HDRLEN` follow the upstream HEV definition. `ATYP` supports IPv4,
.spec/relay-protocol.md-102-IPv6, and domain names. On responses, the address is the source endpoint seen by
.spec/relay-protocol.md:103:the relay. The adapter validates the inner length even though the outer envelope
.spec/relay-protocol.md-104-also has a length.
.spec/relay-protocol.md-105-
.spec/relay-protocol.md:106:`associationID` is allocated by the client and isolates application UDP
.spec/relay-protocol.md:107:associations. The relay maps it to bounded socket state and idle timers. IDs are
.spec/relay-protocol.md:108:not reused within one relay session until a close or expiry has completed.
